---
layout: base.njk
navActive: support
title: "Support Elixir"
description: "Elixir MCP is free to use and independently run. What keeping it going costs, how to sponsor it on GitHub, how running a collector differs from sponsoring, and where the record stands — with nothing for sale."
permalink: /support/index.html
canonical: /support
---
{#-
  The Support page, as the 2026-09-10 design draws it: a rail of five
  anchors on one document (like the Data page used to be, and for the
  same reason the Data page stopped: these five sections are one
  argument, not five destinations), the sponsor button first, then why
  the record matters, what the money pays for, GitHub Sponsors, the
  collector alternative, and the corpus counters.

  The whole page rests on one promise, repeated at the top, in the
  Sponsors panel and at the foot: sponsorship changes nothing about an
  account. Supercell's Fan Content Policy forbids selling access, and
  reading is universal by design (docs/roles). Every number here is
  baked from the same stats endpoint /data reads, so the page can never
  quote a figure the corpus page would contradict.
-#}
{%- set t = stats.totals %}
{%- set n = "—" %}
{%- set sponsorUrl = "https://github.com/sponsors/jthingelstad" %}
{%- set sections = [
  { id: "why", label: "Why it matters", icon: "history" },
  { id: "costs", label: "What it pays for", icon: "receipt" },
  { id: "sponsors", label: "GitHub Sponsors", icon: "heart" },
  { id: "collector", label: "Run a Collector", icon: "server" },
  { id: "record", label: "Where the record stands", icon: "chart-column" }
] %}
<div class="siterail">
  <aside class="siterail__nav" data-siterail data-open="false">
    <button type="button" class="siterail__head" data-rail-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="support-rail">
      <span class="siterail__head-title">Support</span>
      <span class="siterail__head-here" data-rail-here>{{ sections[0].label }}</span>
      <span class="siterail__head-meta">{{ sections.length }}<span class="siterail__head-chevron">{% icon "chevron-down", 17 %}</span></span>
    </button>
    <nav class="siterail__list" id="support-rail" aria-label="On this page" data-rail-anchors>
      <div class="rail__group">On this page</div>
      {%- for s in sections %}
      <a class="rail__item{% if loop.first %} rail__item--on{% endif %}" href="#{{ s.id }}">{% icon s.icon, 18 %}{{ s.label }}</a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </nav>
    <div class="siterail__foot">
      Elixir is free to use. Reading is universal, and sponsorship does not change that.
    </div>
  </aside>

  <div class="siterail__body">
    <h1 class="hero-title" style="font-size: 38px; margin: 0 0 10px">Support Elixir</h1>
    <p class="docs__lede" style="max-width: 60ch; margin-bottom: 22px">
      Elixir is free to use and independently run. Keeping it going takes
      storage, compute, APIs, AI services, and collection that never stops.
      If the record is useful to you, you can help pay for it.
    </p>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 14px">
      <a class="btn btn--gold" href="{{ sponsorUrl }}" rel="noopener">{% icon "heart", 17 %}Sponsor Elixir on GitHub</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/docs/operators">{% icon "server", 17 %}Run a Collector</a>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote" style="font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 30px; max-width: 66ch; text-wrap: pretty">
      Voluntary, and that is the whole arrangement: no extra quota, no longer
      retention, no features, no priority. Supercell&rsquo;s
      <a href="https://www.supercell.com/fan-content-policy">Fan Content Policy</a>
      forbids selling access &mdash; and we would not want to sell it anyway.
    </p>

    {#- Why. The table's right-hand column is the corpus talking: since-date,
        snapshot count and war weeks come from the stats bake, so the
        argument for the archive is made with the archive's own figures. -#}
    <section class="panel" id="why" style="margin-bottom: 22px">
      <div class="panel__head">
        <h2 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0">Clash Royale forgets. Elixir remembers.</h2>
        <a href="/data/collect" style="margin-left: auto; font-size: 13px; white-space: nowrap">What we collect &rsaquo;</a>
      </div>
      <p class="panel__body" style="margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-body); max-width: 74ch; text-wrap: pretty">
        The game&rsquo;s API answers <em style="color: var(--ink)">now</em>. It
        holds the last handful of battles, the current roster, a rolling
        window of war weeks &mdash; and everything older is gone, not archived.
        Elixir records history while it still exists, so the same question
        can be asked next season.
      </p>
      <div class="table__scroll">
        <table class="table" style="min-width: 600px">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>WHAT</th>
              <th>THE GAME&rsquo;S API</th>
              <th>ELIXIR</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td style="color: var(--ink)">Battles</td>
              <td style="color: var(--ink-dim)">about the last 30 per player</td>
              <td>every battle recorded{% if t %} since {{ t.oldest_battle | day }}{% endif %}</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="color: var(--ink)">Player history</td>
              <td style="color: var(--ink-dim)">current snapshot only</td>
              <td>daily snapshots{% if t %} &middot; {{ t.snapshots | number }} so far{% endif %}</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="color: var(--ink)">Trophy progression</td>
              <td style="color: var(--ink-dim)">current and best</td>
              <td>the whole curve, day by day</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="color: var(--ink)">Deck usage</td>
              <td style="color: var(--ink-dim)">not exposed</td>
              <td>derived from recorded battles</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="color: var(--ink)">Clan history</td>
              <td style="color: var(--ink-dim)">current roster</td>
              <td>roster read every 15 minutes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="color: var(--ink)">Clan wars</td>
              <td style="color: var(--ink-dim)">rolling 20 weeks</td>
              <td>{% if t %}{{ t.war_weeks | number }} war weeks and counting{% else %}every war week, past the API&rsquo;s window{% endif %}</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="panel__foot" style="font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-dim); text-wrap: pretty">
        No sponsor owns any part of the record. Sponsorship pays to keep the
        archive running; what is in it belongs to the people and clans who
        asked us to record them.
      </div>
    </section>

    {#- Costs. Six lines, deliberately mundane: the point is that this is a
        bill, not a pitch. -#}
    <section id="costs" style="margin-bottom: 22px">
      <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 4px">What sponsorship pays for</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-faint); margin: 0 0 14px; max-width: 60ch">
        High level, and honestly mundane. This is the bill for keeping a
        record that grows every day.
      </p>
      <div class="stats" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(264px, 1fr))">
        {%- set costs = [
          ["Storage and backups", "database", "The corpus and its point-in-time backups grow every day and never shrink."],
          ["App and API infrastructure", "server", "The hub, the MCP endpoint, this site, and the queues behind them."],
          ["Continuous collection", "radar", "Battle, player, clan and river-race polling that runs every few minutes."],
          ["AI and model usage", "bot", "Agent-facing surfaces and the enrichment that runs over recorded history."],
          ["Monitoring and tooling", "activity", "Alarms, request budgets, the operator console — how a gap gets noticed."],
          ["Long-term retention", "archive", "Keeping history past the point the game's API drops it. That is the point."]
        ] %}
        {%- for c in costs %}
        <div class="stats__cell">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; font-size: 14.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 5px"><span style="color: var(--accent-bright); display: flex">{% icon c[1], 17 %}</span>{{ c[0] }}</div>
          <div style="font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-dim); text-wrap: pretty">{{ c[2] }}</div>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>

    {#- Sponsors. Suggested amounts, not tiers: the word "tier" already
        means something on this site (docs/roles), and these must never be
        confused with it. -#}
    <section class="panel" id="sponsors" style="margin-bottom: 22px; background: var(--panel-float); border-color: rgba(245, 200, 76, 0.42)">
      <div class="panel__head">
        <span style="display: flex; color: var(--gold)">{% icon "heart", 17 %}</span>
        <h2 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0">GitHub Sponsors</h2>
        <span class="mono" style="margin-left: auto; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-faint)">github.com/sponsors/jthingelstad</span>
      </div>
      <p style="padding: 14px 16px 4px; margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-body); max-width: 70ch; text-wrap: pretty">
        Three suggested levels &mdash; not plans, and not a menu. They exist so
        the amount is easy to pick, and nothing about your Elixir account
        changes when you pick one.
      </p>
      <div style="padding: 10px 16px 0">
        {%- set levels = [
          ["Elixir Supporter", "$5 / month", "Help keep Elixir running and preserving Clash Royale history."],
          ["Elixir Steward", "$10 / month", "Cover a steady share of storage, collection and the daily running costs."],
          ["Elixir Sustainer", "$20 / month", "Additional support for the long-term operation and growth of Elixir."]
        ] %}
        {%- for l in levels %}
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 13px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft)">
          <span style="font-size: 14.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); flex: 0 0 auto">{{ l[0] }}</span>
          <span class="mono" style="font-size: 13px; color: var(--gold); flex: 0 0 auto">{{ l[1] }}</span>
          <span style="font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-dim); flex: 1 1 260px; min-width: 0; text-wrap: pretty">{{ l[2] }}</span>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="panel__actions" style="gap: 14px; margin-top: 13px; background: none">
        <a class="btn btn--gold" href="{{ sponsorUrl }}" rel="noopener">{% icon "heart", 17 %}Sponsor Elixir on GitHub</a>
        <span style="font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-faint); flex: 1 1 220px; min-width: 0; text-wrap: pretty">
          Custom amounts and one-off sponsorships work the same way. Cancel
          whenever; nothing you rely on depends on it.
        </span>
      </div>
    </section>

    {#- Collector. The one place on this page where something DOES change an
        account (collectors earn quota), so the separation from sponsorship
        is stated in a callout rather than left to inference. -#}
    <section class="panel" id="collector" style="margin-bottom: 22px; background: var(--panel-float); border-color: var(--line-strong)">
      <div class="panel__head">
        <span style="display: flex; color: var(--accent-bright)">{% icon "server", 17 %}</span>
        <h2 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0">Contribute capacity instead</h2>
        <span class="tag-chip" style="margin-left: auto">Collector</span>
      </div>
      <p style="padding: 14px 16px 0; margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-body); max-width: 72ch; text-wrap: pretty">
        A Collector is a small process you run that fetches Clash Royale data
        on Elixir&rsquo;s behalf and hands it to the hub. More Collectors means
        more of the game recorded, more often. Active Collectors do earn
        additional quota &mdash; that is capacity you contributed coming back
        to you, not a reward for paying.
      </p>
      <div style="margin: 14px 16px; padding: 12px 14px; border-left: 2px solid var(--gold); background: var(--panel); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-body); text-wrap: pretty">
        Sponsorship supports the project financially. Collectors add to
        Elixir&rsquo;s operating capacity. They are separate, and only one of
        them changes what the network can record.
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 0 16px 16px">
        <a class="btn" href="/docs/operators">Collector setup guide {% icon "arrow-right", 15 %}</a>
        <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/status/collectors">Raise your hand in the console</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    {#- The record. The SAME four brand counters as Home and /data, from the
        same bake — a fundraising page that quoted its own numbers would be
        the first place the site contradicted itself. -#}
    <section id="record" style="margin-bottom: 22px">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0">Where the record stands</h2>
        <a href="/data" style="font-size: 13.5px">Full corpus &rsaquo;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stats__cell">
          <div class="label">battles</div>
          <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.battles | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
          <div class="stats__note">{% if t %}since {{ t.oldest_battle | day }}{% else %}recorded{% endif %}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stats__cell">
          <div class="label">players</div>
          <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.players | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
          <div class="stats__note">observed</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stats__cell">
          <div class="label">clans</div>
          <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.clans | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
          <div class="stats__note">observed</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stats__cell">
          <div class="label">war weeks</div>
          <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.war_weeks | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
          <div class="stats__note">recorded races</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="footnote" style="margin: 11px 0 0; max-width: 70ch; text-wrap: pretty">
        Same numbers the Data page reads, from the same statistics endpoint
        &mdash; not a fundraising figure.{% if t %} Captured by
        {{ t.collectors_active | number }} active
        collector{% if t.collectors_active != 1 %}s{% endif %}; the oldest
        recorded battle is from {{ t.oldest_battle | day }}.{% else %} Figures are baked at
        build time and arrive on the next build.{% endif %}
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="panel" style="padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-body); max-width: 76ch; text-wrap: pretty">
      Elixir is a free community project. Sponsorship is optional and gives no
      additional features, quota, retention, or access &mdash; at any amount.
      The record stays the same for everyone reading it.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script defer src="/assets/site-rail.js"></script>
<script defer src="/assets/rail-anchors.js"></script>
